cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the exact Gate A version, evidence-index digest, canonical-report digest,
  and packet Git commit that you reviewed. Cite a distribution receipt only when
  it binds those same bytes. Publisher readback is an assertion unless a distinct
  independent transport record binds the same packet.
title: "Reiyah: HARBOR Gate A Research Architecture"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wahnich
    given-names: Daniel
repository-code: "https://github.com/manfromnowhere143/reiyah"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.2.1
abstract: >-
  A Gate A 1.2.1 documentation, discovery, and lineage continuity architecture
  for the proposed HARBOR research program. It exact-binds the public 1.2.0
  scientific packet as inherited historical evidence and adds only pointer-only,
  evidence-ineligible frontier discovery material. It does not rerun the bound
  scientific handler or create a runtime, empirical result, safety claim,
  standards claim, comparative superiority claim, or operator acceptance.
keywords:
  - automated driving
  - human automation interaction
  - uncertainty
  - causal inference
  - benchmark governance
